\p \v 8 \rb But you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb have departed|סַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the way,|הַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and your instruction|בַּתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb has caused many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to stumble.|הִכְשַׁלְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb You have violated|שִֽׁחַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Levi,”|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb “So I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb in turn|וְגַם־\rb* \rb have made|נָתַ֧תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb you despised|נִבְזִ֥ים\rb* \rb and humiliated|וּשְׁפָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb before all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb because|כְּפִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you have not|אֵֽינְכֶם֙\rb* \rb kept|שֹׁמְרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My ways,|דְּרָכַ֔י\rb* \rb but have shown partiality|וְנֹשְׂאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb in matters of the law.”|בַּתּוֹרָֽה׃פ\rb*
\s1 Judah’s Unfaithfulness
\p \v 10 \rb Do we not|הֲל֨וֹא\rb* \rb all|לְכֻלָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb have one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb Father?|אָ֤ב\rb* \rb Did not|הֲל֛וֹא\rb* \rb one|אֶֽחָ֖ד\rb* \rb God|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb create us?|בְּרָאָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb Why then|מַדּ֗וּעַ\rb* \rb do we break faith|נִבְגַּד֙\rb* \rb with one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|בְּאָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb so as to profane|לְחַלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of our fathers?|אֲבֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb has broken faith;|בָּגְדָ֣ה\rb* \rb an abomination|וְתוֹעֵבָ֛ה\rb* \rb has been committed|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֥ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem.|וּבִירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb has profaned|חִלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb beloved|אָהֵ֔ב\rb* \rb sanctuary|קֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb by marrying|וּבָעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of a foreign|נֵכָֽר׃\rb* \rb god.|אֵ֥ל\rb* \v 12 \rb As for the man|לָאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb does this,|יַעֲשֶׂ֙נָּה֙\rb* \rb may the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb cut off|יַכְרֵ֨ת\rb* \rb from the tents|מֵאָהֳלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb everyone who is awake|עֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and aware—|וְעֹנֶ֔ה\rb*  \rb even if he brings|וּמַגִּ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb an offering|מִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃פ\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb And this|וְזֹאת֙\rb* \rb is another|שֵׁנִ֣ית\rb* \rb thing you do:|תַּֽעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb You cover|כַּסּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb with tears,|דִּמְעָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with weeping|בְּכִ֖י\rb* \rb and groaning,|וַֽאֲנָקָ֑ה\rb* \rb because He no|מֵאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb longer|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb regards|פְּנוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your offerings|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb or receives them|וְלָקַ֥חַת\rb* \rb gladly|רָצ֖וֹן\rb* \rb from your hands.|מִיֶּדְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Yet you ask,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb “Why?”|עַל־\rb*\rb |מָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb It is because|עַ֡ל\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb has been a witness|הֵעִ֨יד\rb* \rb between you|בֵּינְךָ֜\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֣ין׀\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb of your youth,|נְעוּרֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb against whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have broken faith,|בָּגַ֣דְתָּה\rb* \rb though she is|וְהִ֥יא\rb* \rb your companion|חֲבֶרְתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb and your wife|וְאֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb by covenant.|בְּרִיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Has not the LORD|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb made them|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb one,|אֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb having a portion|וּשְׁאָ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Spirit?|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb And why|וּמָה֙\rb* \rb one?|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb Because He seeks|מְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb godly|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb offspring.|זֶ֣רַע\rb* \rb So guard yourselves|וְנִשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb in your spirit|בְּר֣וּחֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and do not|אַל־\rb* \rb break faith|יִבְגֹּֽד׃\rb* \rb with the wife|וּבְאֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb of your youth.|נְעוּרֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb “For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I hate|שָׂנֵ֣א\rb* \rb divorce,”|שַׁלַּ֗ח\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb “He who divorces his wife covers|וְכִסָּ֤ה\rb* \rb his garment|לְבוּשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb violence,”|חָמָס֙\rb*\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Or \fqa “For the man who hates his wife and divorces her,” says the LORD, the God of Israel, “covers his garment with violence,”\f* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb So guard yourselves|וְנִשְׁמַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb in your spirit|בְּרוּחֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb break faith.|תִבְגֹּֽדוּ׃ס\rb*
\b 
\p \v 17 \rb You have wearied|הוֹגַעְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb with your words;|בְּדִבְרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb yet you ask,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb “How|בַּמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have we wearied Him?”|הוֹגָ֑עְנוּ\rb*
\p \rb By saying,|בֶּאֱמָרְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “All|כָּל־\rb* \rb who do|עֹ֨שֵׂה\rb* \rb evil|רָ֜ע\rb* \rb are good|ט֣וֹב׀\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and in them|וּבָהֶם֙\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb delights,”|חָפֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb or,|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb “Where|אַיֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of justice?”|הַמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*
\c 3
\s1 I Will Send My Messenger
\r \ref Matthew 11:7–19|MAT 11:7-19\ref*; \ref Luke 7:24–35|LUK 7:24-35\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “Behold,|הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb I will send|שֹׁלֵחַ֙\rb* \rb My messenger,|מַלְאָכִ֔י\rb* \rb who will prepare|וּפִנָּה־\rb* \rb the way|דֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb before Me.|לְפָנָ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 11:10|MAT 11:10\ref*, Mark 1:2, and Luke 7:27\f* \rb Then the Lord|הָאָד֣וֹן׀\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb seek|מְבַקְשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb will suddenly|וּפִתְאֹם֩\rb* \rb come|יָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb His temple—|הֵיכָל֜וֹ\rb*  \rb the Messenger|וּמַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb of the covenant,|הַבְּרִ֜ית\rb* \rb in whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb delight—|חֲפֵצִים֙\rb*  \rb see,|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb He is coming,”|בָ֔א\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb But who|וּמִ֤י\rb* \rb can endure|מְכַלְכֵּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of His coming?|בּוֹא֔וֹ\rb* \rb And who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can stand|הָעֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb when He appears?|בְּהֵרָֽאוֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He|הוּא֙\rb* \rb will be like a refiner’s|מְצָרֵ֔ף\rb* \rb fire,|כְּאֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb like a launderer’s|מְכַבְּסִֽים׃\rb* \rb soap.|וּכְבֹרִ֖ית\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And He will sit|וְיָשַׁ֨ב\rb* \rb as a refiner|מְצָרֵ֤ף\rb* \rb and purifier|וּמְטַהֵר֙\rb* \rb of silver;|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb He will purify|וְטִהַ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִי֙\rb* \rb and refine|וְזִקַּ֣ק\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb like gold|כַּזָּהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and silver.|וְכַכָּ֑סֶף\rb*\rb |וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb Then they will present|מַגִּישֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb offerings|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in righteousness.|בִּצְדָקָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the offerings|מִנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb will please|וְעָֽרְבָה֙\rb* \rb the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb as in days|כִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of old|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb and years|וּכְשָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb gone by.|קַדְמֹנִיּֽוֹת׃\rb*
\b 
\p \v 5 \rb “Then I will draw near|וְקָרַבְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶם֮\rb* \rb for judgment.|לַמִּשְׁפָּט֒\rb* \rb And I will be|וְהָיִ֣יתִי׀\rb* \rb a swift|מְמַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb witness|עֵ֣ד\rb* \rb against sorcerers|בַּֽמְכַשְּׁפִים֙\rb* \rb and adulterers|וּבַמְנָ֣אֲפִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וּבַנִּשְׁבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb perjurers,|לַשָּׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb against oppressors|וּבְעֹשְׁקֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the widowed|אַלְמָנָ֨ה\rb* \rb and fatherless,|וְיָת֤וֹם\rb* \rb and against those who defraud laborers|שְׂכַר־\rb* \rb of their wages|שָׂ֠כִיר\rb* \rb and deny justice|וּמַטֵּי־\rb* \rb to the foreigner|גֵר֙\rb* \rb but do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb fear Me,”|יְרֵא֔וּנִי\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*
\s1 Robbing God
\p \v 6 \rb “Because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I,|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb change,|שָׁנִ֑יתִי\rb* \rb you|וְאַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb descendants|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb been destroyed.|כְלִיתֶֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Yet from the days|לְמִימֵ֨י\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb you have turned away|סַרְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb from My statutes|מֵֽחֻקַּי֙\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb kept them.|שְׁמַרְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb Return|שׁ֤וּבוּ\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb and I will return|וְאָשׁ֣וּבָה\rb* \rb to you,”|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*
\p \rb “But you ask,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb ‘How|בַּמֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb can we return?’|נָשֽׁוּב׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Will a man|אָדָ֜ם\rb* \rb rob|הֲיִקְבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb God?|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb Yet|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb are robbing|קֹבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb Me!|אֹתִ֔י\rb*
\p \rb But you ask,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb ‘How|בַּמֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb do we rob You?’|קְבַעֲנ֑וּךָ\rb*
\p \rb In tithes|הַֽמַּעֲשֵׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and offerings.|וְהַתְּרוּמָֽה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb are cursed|נֵֽאָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְאֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb with a curse,|בַּמְּאֵרָה֙\rb* \rb yet you—|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb the whole|כֻּלּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb nation—|הַגּ֖וֹי\rb* \rb are still robbing Me.|קֹבְעִ֑ים\rb* \v 10 \rb Bring|הָבִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the full|כָּל־\rb* \rb tithe|הַֽמַּעֲשֵׂ֜ר\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the storehouse,|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הָאוֹצָ֗ר\rb* \rb so that there may be|וִיהִ֥י\rb* \rb food|טֶ֙רֶף֙\rb* \rb in My house.|בְּבֵיתִ֔י\rb* \rb Test Me|וּבְחָנ֤וּנִי\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb in this,”|בָּזֹ֔את\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb “See if|אִם־\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb open|אֶפְתַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the windows|אֲרֻבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and pour out|וַהֲרִיקֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb blessing|בְּרָכָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb without|בְּלִי־\rb* \rb measure.|דָֽי׃\rb*\f + \fr 3:10 \ft Literally \fqa blessing for which there will be no room\f* \v 11 \rb I will rebuke|וְגָעַרְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb the devourer|בָּֽאֹכֵ֔ל\rb*\f + \fr 3:11 \fqa The devourer \ft is probably a name for a crop-destroying pest.\f* \rb for you,|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb so that it will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb destroy|יַשְׁחִ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fruits|פְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of your land,|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and the vine|הַגֶּ֙פֶן֙\rb* \rb in your field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb fail to produce fruit,”|תְשַׁכֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb “Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb will call you blessed,|וְאִשְּׁר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb will be|תִהְי֤וּ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of delight,”|חֵ֔פֶץ\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Book of Remembrance
\p \v 13 \rb “Your words|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against Me|עָלַ֛י\rb* \rb have been harsh,”|חָזְק֥וּ\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “Yet you ask,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb ‘What|מַה־\rb* \rb have we spoken|נִּדְבַּ֖רְנוּ\rb* \rb against You?’|עָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb You have said,|אֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb ‘It is futile|שָׁ֖וְא\rb* \rb to serve|עֲבֹ֣ד\rb* \rb God.|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb have we gained|בֶּ֗צַע\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb by keeping|שָׁמַ֙רְנוּ֙\rb* \rb His requirements|מִשְׁמַרְתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְכִ֤י\rb* \rb and walking|הָלַ֙כְנוּ֙\rb* \rb mournfully|קְדֹ֣רַנִּ֔ית\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts?|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 15 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb call the arrogant|זֵדִ֑ים\rb* \rb blessed.|מְאַשְּׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb Not only|גַּם־\rb* \rb do evildoers|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb*\rb |רִשְׁעָ֔ה\rb* \rb prosper,|נִבְנוּ֙\rb* \rb they even|גַּ֧ם\rb* \rb test|בָּחֲנ֛וּ\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and escape.’”|וַיִּמָּלֵֽטוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb At that time|אָ֧ז\rb* \rb those who feared|יִרְאֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb spoke|נִדְבְּר֛וּ\rb* \rb with one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb another,|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb listened|וַיַּקְשֵׁ֤ב\rb* \rb and heard them.|וַיִּשְׁמָ֔ע\rb* \rb So a scroll|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of remembrance|זִכָּר֤וֹן\rb* \rb was written|וַ֠יִּכָּתֵב\rb* \rb before Him|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb regarding those who feared|לְיִרְאֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and honored|וּלְחֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb His name.|שְׁמֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb “They will be|וְהָ֣יוּ\rb* \rb Mine,”|לִ֗י\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb “on the day|לַיּ֕וֹם\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb prepare|עֹשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb My treasured possession.|סְגֻלָּ֑ה\rb* \rb And I will spare|וְחָמַלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb spares|יַחְמֹ֣ל\rb* \rb his own|עַל־\rb* \rb son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb who serves|הָעֹבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb him.|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 18 \rb So you will again|וְשַׁבְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb distinguish|וּרְאִיתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the righteous|צַדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb and the wicked,|לְרָשָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb those who serve|עֹבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and those who|לַאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb do not.”|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |עֲבָדֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\c 4
\s1 The Day of the LORD
\r \ref Zephaniah 1:7–18|ZEP 1:7-18\ref*; \ref 1 Thessalonians 5:1–11|1TH 5:1-11\ref*; \ref 2 Peter 3:8–13|2PE 3:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb is coming,|בָּ֔א\rb* \rb burning|בֹּעֵ֖ר\rb* \rb like a furnace,|כַּתַּנּ֑וּר\rb* \rb when|וְהָי֨וּ\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the arrogant|זֵדִ֜ים\rb* \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb evildoer|עֹשֵׂ֤ה\rb*\rb |רִשְׁעָה֙\rb* \rb will be stubble;|קַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb is coming|הַבָּ֗א\rb* \rb when I will set them ablaze,”|וְלִהַ֨ט\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb “Not|לֹא־\rb* \rb a root|שֹׁ֥רֶשׁ\rb* \rb or branch|וְעָנָֽף׃\rb* \rb will be left|יַעֲזֹ֥ב\rb* \rb to them.”|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb “But for you who fear|יִרְאֵ֤י\rb* \rb My name,|שְׁמִי֙\rb* \rb the sun|שֶׁ֣מֶשׁ\rb* \rb of righteousness|צְדָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb will rise|וְזָרְחָ֨ה\rb* \rb with healing|וּמַרְפֵּ֖א\rb* \rb in its wings,|בִּכְנָפֶ֑יהָ\rb*\f + \fr 4:2 \ft Or \fqa the Sun of Righteousness will rise with healing in His wings\f* \rb and you will go out|וִֽיצָאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and leap|וּפִשְׁתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb like calves|כְּעֶגְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb from the stall.|מַרְבֵּֽק׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Then you will trample|וְעַסּוֹתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb the wicked,|רְשָׁעִ֔ים\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they will be|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb ashes|אֵ֔פֶר\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the soles|כַּפּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of your feet|רַגְלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb on the day|בַּיּוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am preparing,”|עֹשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָאֽוֹת׃פ\rb*
\b 
\p \v 4 \rb “Remember|זִכְר֕וּ\rb* \rb the law|תּוֹרַ֖ת\rb* \rb of My servant|עַבְדִּ֑י\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the statutes|חֻקִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטִֽים׃\rb* \rb I commanded|צִוִּ֨יתִי\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb at Horeb.|בְחֹרֵב֙\rb*\f + \fr 4:4 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f*
\p \v 5 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will send|שֹׁלֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֗י\rb* \rb the coming|בּ֚וֹא\rb* \rb of the great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָֽא׃\rb*\f + \fr 4:5 \ft Or \fqa dreadful\ft ; LXX \fqa glorious\f* \rb Day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \v 6 \rb And he will turn|וְהֵשִׁ֤יב\rb* \rb the hearts|לֵב־\rb* \rb of the fathers|אָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their children,|בָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and the hearts|וְלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of the children|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their fathers.|אֲבוֹתָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Cited in \ref Luke 1:17|LUK 1:17\ref*\f* \rb Otherwise,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb I will come|אָב֕וֹא\rb* \rb and strike|וְהִכֵּיתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb with a curse.”|חֵֽרֶם׃\rb*
